      <body>
         <div type="edition" xml:lang="kaw-Latn" rendition="class:38769 maturity:83213">
            <p>
<lb n="1"/>kitrinira hurip·
<lb n="2"/>hañar kabuyutan·
<lb n="3"/>barabaṁ syala kakaliḥ
            </p>
         </div>
         <div type="apparatus">
               <listApp>
                <app loc="2">
                    <lem>hañar</lem>
                    <rdg source="bib:Groeneveldt1887_01">haneṁ</rdg>
		     <rdg source="bib:Crucq1929_01">hane</rdg>
			<note>While the reading <foreign>ñ</foreign> instead of <foreign>n</foreign> is not self-evident, it is clear that there is neither <foreign>taling</foreign> nor <foreign>cecak</foreign>.</note>
                     </app>
		<app loc="3">
			<lem>barabaṁ syala kakaliḥ</lem>
			<rdg source="bib:Crucq1929_01">baravaṁs pala kakaliḥ</rdg>
	<note>The characters between <foreign>barabaṁ</foreign> and <foreign>kakaliḥ</foreign> were left unread by Brandes. The solution proposed by Crucq, after consultation with Poerbatjaraka, is implausible.</note>
</app>
               </listApp>
         </div>
         <div type="translation" resp="part:argr">
            <p>Meritorious work of Hurip Hanyar, hermitage of Barabang, both stones.</p>
         </div>
	  <div type="translation" xml:lang="nld-Latn" source="bib:Crucq1929_01">
            <p>Een levend gedenkteeken op een heilige plaats, dragende twee vruchten.</p>
         </div>

         <div type="commentary">
            <!--commentary encoded as per section §9.3 -->
         </div>
        <div type="bibliography">
           <p>A preliminary reading was communicated by Brandes (footnote to <bibl><ptr target="bib:Groeneveldt1887_01"/></bibl>); the text was reconsidered by Crucq (<bibl rend="omitname"><ptr target="bib:Crucq1929_01"/></bibl>), in consultation with Poerbatjaraka. The present digital edition was established from photograph <ref target="http://hdl.handle.net/1887.1/item:4102844">OD 6516</ref> and from a photograph of the estampage OD-BRIN 194.</p>
